meta {
  name: Update a post
  type: http
  seq: 40
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/posts/:id
  body: json
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  seed: 1
  ~locale: 
  ~conflict: 
  ~delay: 
  ~trickle: 
  ~status: 
  ~fail: 
  ~auth: 
}

params:path {
  id: 1
}

body:json {
  {
    "userId": 7204,
    "title": "95bl",
    "body": "pGcS1Fp"
  }
}

docs {
  Validates the fields sent and answers with the post merged with them, with `updatedAt` set.

  `userId` must name a record in `/users` at the same `seed` and `locale`, or the write answers `422`. With the session on, deleting a post also deletes the comments that point at it, and theirs in turn.

  By default nothing is stored, so a later read returns the same data as before and the response is what the write would have produced. With the session on (`--session`, `REST_IN_PIECES_SESSION=true` or `createApp({ session: true })`), the change is kept in memory and later reads at the same `seed` and `locale` see it, until `POST /reset`. A session that is full answers `507`.
}
